---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { ArrowLeft, AlertCircle } from 'lucide-react';
---

<Layout title="Usage Disclaimer">
  <div class="p-6 md:p-8 max-w-4xl mx-auto w-full space-y-6 animate-in fade-in duration-200">
    {/* Navigation header */}
    <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-hairline-soft pb-4">
      <a href="/dashboard" class="flex items-center gap-1 text-xs font-bold text-steel hover:text-primary transition">
        <ArrowLeft className="w-3.5 h-3.5" /> Back to Dashboard
      </a>
      <span class="text-[9px] uppercase tracking-wider font-bold text-slate-400">Classified // Internal Use Only</span>
    </div>

    {/* Document Container */}
    <div class="bg-canvas border border-hairline-soft p-6 md:p-10 rounded-xxxl card-product-shadow space-y-6">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-circle bg-primary/10 flex items-center justify-center text-primary">
          <AlertCircle className="w-5 h-5" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-steel font-bold">KSP-ConAI Compliance</span>
          <h1 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink-deep">Usage & Intelligence Disclaimer</h1>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="text-[11px] text-stone font-medium">
        Last Updated: July 2026 | Authority: Karnataka State Police Director General
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-5 text-xs text-steel leading-relaxed">
        <section class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink-deep">1. Advisory Nature of AI Tools</h2>
          <p>
            The Karnataka State Police Crime Intelligence Copilot (KSP-ConAI) utilizes Large Language Models (LLMs), machine learning algorithms, and natural language processing to assist officers in analyzing Case Narrative Diaries, establishing suspect timelines, and generating suspect relationship graphs.
          </p>
          <p class="font-bold text-ink-deep">
            All AI-generated summaries, chat responses, and relationship links are advisory in nature. They do NOT constitute official legal testimony, final evidence, or deterministic assertions of guilt.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink-deep">2. Officer Verification Requirement</h2>
          <p>
            Investigating Officers (IOs) bear sole legal responsibility for the accuracy and validity of their case files. All intelligence outputs produced by KSP-ConAI must be:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
            <li>Cross-checked against the official signed paper Case Diaries and CCTNS records.</li>
            <li>Verified with original witness statements and forensic reports before submission to a court of law.</li>
            <li>Confirmed for accuracy in names, dates, sections, and recovery amounts.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink-deep">3. Geolocation and Mapping Limitations</h2>
          <p>
            Hotspots maps, cluster zones, and coordinate pins rendered on this platform are based on available address texts and mobile tower records. They represent statistical approximations rather than exact physical locations. Discrepancies in street maps or boundaries should be resolved using official municipal records.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink-deep">4. No Legal Liability</h2>
          <p>
            The Government of Karnataka and the Karnataka State Police Command Centre decline all liability for errors, processing offsets, or procedural delays caused by reliance on KSP-ConAI's automated intelligence feeds.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <div class="border-t border-hairline-soft pt-4 flex justify-between items-center text-[10px] text-stone">
        <span>KSP-ConAI Protocol V1.0</span>
        <button onclick="window.print()" class="text-primary hover:underline font-bold cursor-pointer">Print Document</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
